course: dictionary
lesson: 3719
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is right by reading the words around the word. This is its context. The word flier is a good example.
explain: «Part one is about animals and where they live: the biggest cat, the fastest flier, the longest traveller.» Here a flier is a creature that flies, such as a bird. The other words, animals and where they live, are the clue.
explain: Flier can also be a sheet of paper that advertises something. Shops hand out fliers, and people put them through letterboxes. In that sense, the clue is words like advertising or letterbox. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one. If it does not, try the next meaning.
fact: A flier is a person or thing that flies, such as a pilot, a bird or a passenger on a plane.
fact: A flier is also a sheet of paper advertising something. This is more often spelled flyer.
fact: «The largest fliers ever, pterosaurs like Quetzalcoatlus, had wings about 10 metres across but were light, with hollow bones.»
fact: In the phrase «get off to a flier», flier is an informal word for a very quick start.
fact: Other phrases you may hear are «a high flier», meaning someone very successful, and «frequent flier», meaning someone who travels by plane often.
exercise: «Part one is about animals: the fastest flier, the longest traveller.» What does flier mean here? | *Something that flies, such as a bird | A letter sent by post | A fast runner on the track | A sheet of paper advertising a sale
exercise: A shop puts a flier through Mum's letterbox. What is a flier in this sentence? | *A sheet of paper advertising something | A bird that has landed on the step | A parcel for the family | A pilot in a cockpit
exercise: Dad says, «She got off to a flier in the race.» What does this mean? | *She started very quickly | She lost the race | She flew off in a plane | She ran backwards
test: A pizza shop puts a flier through your letterbox. What is the flier? | A bill from the bank | A lost pet poster that is not for sale | *A paper advert for the shop | A kind of small plane
test: «She is a high flier at work.» What does high flier mean? | *Someone very successful | Someone who is always late | A bird that flies high in the sky | Someone who climbs very high trees
exam: Which of these is NOT a meaning of flier? | *A fish that swims in a river | A pilot or a passenger on a plane | A sheet of paper advertising something | A bird or other creature that flies
